[
    {
        "id": "tix-note",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "tix-tab",
        "name": "Read printed text after barcode-locate (text-inspect reads, it does not grade)",
        "info": "Point `frame` at a camera frame on the Node-RED host, then open\n`text inspect`, load the last frame (press Inject once first) and drag a\nbox around each printed line you want read. The two regions shipped here\nare placeholders.\n\n`barcode-locate` must have Preview OFF here: with Preview on it replaces\nmsg.payload with the barcode's preview crop, and text-inspect would then\nread the crop, not the frame.\n\n`barcode-locate` sends one message per barcode it found (one with\ntext null when it found none), so text-inspect reads the frame once per\nmessage. A msg.regions on the way in would pass through barcode-locate\nand replace text-inspect's own regions.\n\nmsg.ocr carries { name, roi, text, confidences } per region. Nothing\nhere compares the printed text with the barcode data; add that\ndownstream if you need a verdict.",
        "x": 330,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
